1 - ensure Docker desktop is installed locally on your workstation/laptop
2 - copy all files from root to local folder
3 - copy my-app and server-folder to local folder
4 - copy modules folder to local folder
5 - create a folder /data , /logs and /modules
2 - open PowerShell and execute the following commands :
    - docker build --build-arg NPM_FONTAWESOME_TOKEN=--your_npm_token -t wolffie:latest .
    - docker save wolffie:latest -o C:\website\myAlphaESS\wolffie-latest.tar
3 - copy your locally saved docker image to your docker container (NAS)
